WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.116 --> 00:00:02.148
- You always just have to be somebody

00:00:02.148 --> 00:00:03.582
who really loves what you're doing

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:04.993
and make an affordable step.

00:00:04.993 --> 00:00:08.090
Dedicate a certain amount
of time to the business.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.973
Two hours a week, four hours a week,

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:11.877
50 hours a week, no matter what.

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:13.230
A lot of times I want to think

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.455
what am I promising the consumer?

00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:17.278
When the needle is finally in the vein

00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:20.517
and you're really hooked,
it's like being in love.

00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:21.991
I have this little gamble theory,

00:00:21.991 --> 00:00:23.957
if nobody else likes
it, it might be a hit.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:27.411
Can't dribble a basketball,
can't sing, can't draw,

00:00:27.411 --> 00:00:29.385
didn't know anybody, didn't go to college,

00:00:29.385 --> 00:00:30.376
that didn't stop me at all.

00:00:30.376 --> 00:00:32.107
I need a job!

00:00:32.107 --> 00:00:36.442
Really good designer,
I will make you money.

00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:37.987
- He's an American entrepreneur,

00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:42.242
investor, TV personality,
author, and motivational speaker.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:45.806
He's best known as the founder,
president and CEO of FUBU.

00:00:45.806 --> 00:00:47.025
He appears as an investor

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:50.229
on the ABC reality TV show Shark Tank.

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:52.104
He's Daymond John, and here is my take

00:00:52.104 --> 00:00:53.903
on his Top 10 rules for success.

00:00:53.903 --> 00:00:55.819
Rule number four is my personal favorite

00:00:55.819 --> 00:00:57.813
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:57.813 --> 00:01:00.396
for some special bonus footage.

00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:06.645
- And the thing that all
entrepreneurs have in common

00:01:06.645 --> 00:01:11.057
is every entrepreneur makes
an affordable step forward,

00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:13.251
no matter what direction it is,

00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:16.042
then they learn from
that and they repeat it.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.322
That means that when you're
in the dark, you can't see,

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:20.725
you make a small step, you
feel around, you keep going,

00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:23.269
or you step back because
you stepped on something.

00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:27.070
And that's the first one, two,
three, four years of business

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.142
entrepreneurs make the affordable step.

00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:30.775
The other people who are not entrepreneurs

00:01:30.775 --> 00:01:35.725
who are doing it for money make
sometimes unfortunate steps.

00:01:35.725 --> 00:01:37.478
They go and they say I need
to get a million dollars

00:01:37.478 --> 00:01:38.831
cause that's going to cure the problem.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.294
Now you've got a million dollar problem.

00:01:40.294 --> 00:01:42.145
Or they make bad steps because

00:01:42.145 --> 00:01:44.380
they want to go get money because

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.221
they just want to go get
money, they want the Benz

00:01:46.221 --> 00:01:47.463
and all of a sudden they
end up in a place that

00:01:47.463 --> 00:01:49.094
they don't want to be or sometimes

00:01:49.094 --> 00:01:50.806
they end up not existing at all.

00:01:50.806 --> 00:01:53.117
So, you always just have to be

00:01:53.117 --> 00:01:54.986
somebody who really
loves what you're doing

00:01:54.986 --> 00:01:57.418
and make and affordable step forward

00:01:57.418 --> 00:01:59.209
and learn and then repeat.

00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:02.486
Dedicate a certain amount
of time to the business.

00:02:02.486 --> 00:02:04.163
Two hours a week, four hours a week,

00:02:04.163 --> 00:02:06.073
50 hours a week, no matter what,

00:02:06.073 --> 00:02:08.320
it starts to compound after year one,

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.974
after year two, after year three.

00:02:09.974 --> 00:02:12.352
If you dedicated two hours a week to

00:02:12.352 --> 00:02:14.693
this new hobby or love or

00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:18.860
business, at the end of the
year it's over 100 hours put in.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.865
Don't be in a rush, first of all.

00:02:21.865 --> 00:02:23.786
Learn all the mistakes early.

00:02:23.786 --> 00:02:27.026
And then, have some kind of strategy.

00:02:27.026 --> 00:02:28.616
Know that this is where you want to be

00:02:28.616 --> 00:02:30.316
after year one, two, three, four, and five

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.447
and you have to be really
honest with yourself.

00:02:32.447 --> 00:02:35.245
Is the business worth it?
Is it costing too much?

00:02:35.245 --> 00:02:36.858
At the end of the day a lot of times

00:02:36.858 --> 00:02:40.074
people think inwardly about
their company or their product.

00:02:40.074 --> 00:02:41.357
A lot of times I want to think

00:02:41.357 --> 00:02:44.300
What am I promising the consumer?

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.133
And how will I deliver that promise?

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.451
I have to think about what's in it for

00:02:48.451 --> 00:02:49.757
that end of the day person who's going to

00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:50.907
come out of their pocket and buy it,

00:02:50.907 --> 00:02:54.175
so what am I promising, how
am I going to deliver it,

00:02:54.175 --> 00:02:57.031
and now, do I have the assets
to deliver it accurately?

00:02:57.031 --> 00:02:58.494
What changed in my life wasn't

00:02:58.494 --> 00:03:00.641
the fact that I wanted
to become a millionaire.

00:03:00.641 --> 00:03:02.238
What changed in my life was the fact that

00:03:02.238 --> 00:03:04.235
I wanted to make these clothes for myself,

00:03:04.235 --> 00:03:06.562
for other people, because
nobody respected the smart kid.

00:03:06.562 --> 00:03:07.979
I was doing something I loved

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:10.626
and then all of a sudden
it started to take off.

00:03:10.626 --> 00:03:12.542
- [Man] Can you tell me a little bit about

00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:14.457
once that passion finally caught on,

00:03:14.457 --> 00:03:16.338
and you finally decided this is something

00:03:16.338 --> 00:03:17.813
that I want to move forward with.

00:03:17.813 --> 00:03:19.368
And a little bit about that first product,

00:03:19.368 --> 00:03:21.719
and how it all took off from there.

00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:23.786
And then did you ever
decide at that point,

00:03:23.786 --> 00:03:25.344
there was no slowing you down?

00:03:25.344 --> 00:03:29.550
- When that passion, when
that thing grabs ahold of you,

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.808
and as they say when the
needle is finally in the vein,

00:03:31.808 --> 00:03:35.568
and you're really hooked,
it's like being in love.

00:03:35.568 --> 00:03:39.476
It's like you thought you
liked somebody when you were

00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:42.426
13, 14 years old and that was just

00:03:42.426 --> 00:03:44.794
something new and it was puppy love.

00:03:44.794 --> 00:03:47.076
But when you're 22, 23 years old

00:03:47.076 --> 00:03:49.072
and you're out there sitting there

00:03:49.072 --> 00:03:50.791
making life decisions and saying

00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:53.082
I could see myself with this
person for the rest of my life,

00:03:53.082 --> 00:03:55.091
and you're getting butterflies
every time you see them,

00:03:55.091 --> 00:03:56.676
that's what it is when you have a business

00:03:56.676 --> 00:03:58.835
and you have a company that you love,

00:03:58.835 --> 00:04:00.800
you can't see anything else.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.570
And I would've dressed people
til today, for free if I could

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.509
and I'm sure you hear
that from everybody else,

00:04:07.509 --> 00:04:11.676
an artist will rap and sing
anytime they can be seen,

00:04:12.542 --> 00:04:14.115
and just like the kids in school

00:04:14.115 --> 00:04:15.943
who always got kicked out in
Special Ed who were comedians,

00:04:15.943 --> 00:04:19.037
they can't help it, they know
that that's the biggest bully

00:04:19.037 --> 00:04:21.475
in the schoolyard and they can't help it,

00:04:21.475 --> 00:04:23.124
but crack a joke even
though they're going to get

00:04:23.124 --> 00:04:24.790
their head cracked open,

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.073
but they just love what they're doing.

00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:27.611
And that's just how it was as a business.

00:04:27.611 --> 00:04:30.595
I fell in love with FUBU
when I saw that first person

00:04:30.595 --> 00:04:32.586
walking down the street
with my product on.

00:04:32.586 --> 00:04:36.411
Many entrepreneurs fail
due to over funding,

00:04:36.411 --> 00:04:38.048
so you look, we're in
a beautiful location,

00:04:38.048 --> 00:04:40.910
Trattoria Il Mulino,
it's a legendary family

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.884
in the restaurant business,

00:04:42.884 --> 00:04:44.788
and they've been doing this for years.

00:04:44.788 --> 00:04:47.487
But look at somebody that
decides that they can cook

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.711
and they want to work on grandma's recipe.

00:04:49.711 --> 00:04:51.464
They'll go out and they'll
get a $100,000 loan,

00:04:51.464 --> 00:04:52.863
they'll open up a restaurant,

00:04:52.863 --> 00:04:54.355
they have no experience doing that,

00:04:54.355 --> 00:04:56.601
they'll have a beautiful
place, great staff,

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.691
but they didn't sell not one piece of food

00:04:58.691 --> 00:05:00.549
in their entire life, and
they didn't understand

00:05:00.549 --> 00:05:02.133
the operation of the business.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.219
Eight months in, a year in,

00:05:03.219 --> 00:05:05.674
when they realize why they
don't have any customers

00:05:05.674 --> 00:05:07.555
because they didn't have a
customer base in the beginning,

00:05:07.555 --> 00:05:09.720
they have a $100,000
loan now on the business,

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.195
and they haven't figured out the business.

00:05:11.195 --> 00:05:13.314
Then all of a sudden
they have to close down.

00:05:13.314 --> 00:05:16.170
I started off literally
with $800 worth of hats,

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.714
and that was the beginning.

00:05:17.714 --> 00:05:20.193
- Take inventory of yourself.

00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:22.248
That sounds very kum ba yah.

00:05:22.248 --> 00:05:24.993
- It is but you know what, it's very hard.

00:05:24.993 --> 00:05:25.963
You have to sit there and say

00:05:25.963 --> 00:05:28.401
where am I good, where do I have assets

00:05:28.401 --> 00:05:29.753
and where do I have liabilities?

00:05:29.753 --> 00:05:31.089
Who do I know that can help me with this?

00:05:31.089 --> 00:05:32.842
First of all, how much time will I have,

00:05:32.842 --> 00:05:35.053
how much money will I have
to dedicate towards this?

00:05:35.053 --> 00:05:36.603
What am I good at?

00:05:36.603 --> 00:05:39.575
What do I hate and who
will I have to hire?

00:05:39.575 --> 00:05:41.619
You know, a mom does that all day.

00:05:41.619 --> 00:05:42.954
She looks at what we have to cook,

00:05:42.954 --> 00:05:44.434
she looks at what time do we have

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:45.862
to get the kids to school, get them home,

00:05:45.862 --> 00:05:48.713
when I have my own time with
my husband or everything else,

00:05:48.713 --> 00:05:50.663
you have to take inventory of yourself

00:05:50.663 --> 00:05:51.846
or you don't know what you have.

00:05:51.846 --> 00:05:55.763
I think that there's four
levels that any brand

00:05:56.883 --> 00:05:59.077
or product can go through.

00:05:59.077 --> 00:06:00.610
They won't all hit the four levels,

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.040
so you can have an item, and that item is

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.879
alright, I'm making bottled water.

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:08.185
And water can be getting anywhere

00:06:08.185 --> 00:06:10.472
from the fountain, to the stream
or you put it in a bottle.

00:06:10.472 --> 00:06:12.475
You can then have a label,
you put any label on there

00:06:12.475 --> 00:06:13.852
because you go into the store and you say

00:06:13.852 --> 00:06:14.938
well that's bottled water,

00:06:14.938 --> 00:06:16.644
I don't know the label's name, persay.

00:06:16.644 --> 00:06:19.144
Then you have more of a brand.

00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:22.524
Dasani. It's a brand, we
don't know much about it,

00:06:22.524 --> 00:06:24.463
but then you can become a lifestyle.

00:06:24.463 --> 00:06:26.741
Evian. Vitamin Water.

00:06:26.741 --> 00:06:29.959
So, a lot of us don't get
to the level of lifestyle

00:06:29.959 --> 00:06:32.364
where if you copy a piece of paper,

00:06:32.364 --> 00:06:33.772
somebody might say go Xerox it,

00:06:33.772 --> 00:06:35.467
when really, Xerox is a company.

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:38.381
Or you ask for a soda and
somebody calls it a Coke.

00:06:38.381 --> 00:06:41.226
Where it basically categorizes everything.

00:06:41.226 --> 00:06:43.362
You search for something
and they say "Google it,"

00:06:43.362 --> 00:06:46.734
no matter how you're searching
and that becomes a lifestyle.

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:49.874
It's a challenge to go
through those processes

00:06:49.874 --> 00:06:53.041
and what I do with all my companies is

00:06:53.926 --> 00:06:55.941
I say to them that the easiest thing

00:06:55.941 --> 00:06:58.976
to sell in the world is the truth.

00:06:58.976 --> 00:07:01.646
Back in the days it was
make it they will come,

00:07:01.646 --> 00:07:06.232
and we can put some lipstick
on a pig and dress it up.

00:07:06.232 --> 00:07:08.073
With this world of transparency today

00:07:08.073 --> 00:07:11.794
you can create the biggest
lie campaign that you like

00:07:11.794 --> 00:07:13.947
but one person at your office
is going to send out a tweet

00:07:13.947 --> 00:07:18.080
and say it's all garbage and you're over.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.455
So, if you understand that the

00:07:20.455 --> 00:07:23.787
easiest thing to sell is the
truth and you know your DNA,

00:07:23.787 --> 00:07:25.638
if you put that out there then people will

00:07:25.638 --> 00:07:27.833
understand it and people will respect it.

00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:29.441
Or at least if you lose, you know they

00:07:29.441 --> 00:07:32.053
just weren't feeling you
but you know what it was.

00:07:32.053 --> 00:07:33.382
I have a gut feeling that

00:07:33.382 --> 00:07:35.733
this may be very, very good business

00:07:35.733 --> 00:07:38.584
but it's not something that
I can go to sleep at night,

00:07:38.584 --> 00:07:41.672
then it's not even a question,
I won't do it, number one.

00:07:41.672 --> 00:07:43.872
Number two is the risk assessment is

00:07:43.872 --> 00:07:47.146
a lot of times, I have
this little gamble theory,

00:07:47.146 --> 00:07:49.793
if nobody else likes
it, it might be a hit.

00:07:49.793 --> 00:07:52.794
If it's not a lot of money or time,

00:07:52.794 --> 00:07:55.029
I'm going to take a gamble
on it because usually you get

00:07:55.029 --> 00:07:58.442
the lowest common denominator
if everybody agrees.

00:07:58.442 --> 00:08:00.643
The people that I see
utilize "The Power of Broke"

00:08:00.643 --> 00:08:04.631
more than anybody at
all are the people that,

00:08:04.631 --> 00:08:07.196
when they reach a level of
success, they still use it

00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:10.081
and that's how they
maintain their success,

00:08:10.081 --> 00:08:11.242
that hunger and drive.

00:08:11.242 --> 00:08:13.797
And we grew up at a time
and age where it was

00:08:13.797 --> 00:08:16.120
you need money to make money,
you got to know somebody.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.422
Well, look at me, look at half this room.

00:08:19.422 --> 00:08:22.707
I grew up African American, short,

00:08:22.707 --> 00:08:24.924
dyslexic, got left back one time,

00:08:24.924 --> 00:08:26.671
almost got left back a second time,

00:08:26.671 --> 00:08:30.671
can't dribble a basketball,
can't sing, can't draw,

00:08:30.671 --> 00:08:32.668
didn't know anybody, didn't go to college,

00:08:32.668 --> 00:08:33.864
that didn't stop me at all.

00:08:33.864 --> 00:08:34.697
- Yeah.

00:08:34.697 --> 00:08:36.870
- I had a mother that
really loved me dearly,

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:40.040
and I had some like-minded
FUBU partners and friends

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.368
who would never let me stop
and I never let them stop.

00:08:42.368 --> 00:08:44.057
And I had a will and a drive

00:08:44.057 --> 00:08:46.599
and I still have all those same things,

00:08:46.599 --> 00:08:49.096
I still rise and grind
every single morning.

